  "note": "Brief 026 phase 1 (Latch, 2026-10-19): the fixed baseline stops, re-shot every round on identical frames. Points are plan coordinates [x, y] (Unity x, z) at the street datum. Shot kinds: play = the play camera (orthographic, zoom 14, pitch 38, the shot's yaw, centred on the stop's focus, standing back the host's standOff 160 m; TacticalShadows fitted to that depth, ArchitectureFade about the focus, both copied from the scene's cameras/play); follow = the player's follow view (HostFollow and CamPreset defaults: an agent's feet at `pivot` [x, y, height; height default 0.18, the kerbed pavement] facing `yaw`, camera 5.5 m behind and 1.3 + 0.32 x 5.5 m above the feet, looking 8 m ahead at 1.35 m, fov 55, near 0.2, far 600, tactical shadows off so the URP asset's own shadow distance); eye = a perspective camera at `eye` [x, y, height] looking at `look`, with an optional shadowDistance override (m) for views no play camera takes. Each shot's `camera` is pinned by the tool (Suborned/Render/Baseline Shots, Suborned.World.Review.Baseline) the first time it resolves, and every later round renders the pinned camera verbatim, so a change to the rig cannot move a frame; delete a `camera` (or run with -repin) to resolve it again. `capture` records how the last baseline was made: the scene's export stamp, the light and look files' sha256, the sun, ambient, fog, URP asset and the post volume as the player gets them. Nothing here changes lighting, materials or the world.",
